      "stem": "Chloroplasts are gently broken open and separated into two fractions. Fraction 1 consists of stacks of flattened membrane sacs; fraction 2 is the surrounding fluid. When illuminated, fraction 1 releases O<sub>2</sub> and makes ATP and NADPH but does not fix CO<sub>2</sub>. Fraction 2 contains rubisco and can fix CO<sub>2</sub> only if ATP and NADPH are supplied. Which identification is correct?",
