      "explanation": "Correct: (D) Ligand binding promotes GDP being exchanged for GTP on the G protein. In a G protein-coupled receptor pathway, the ligand binds the receptor and changes its shape. The changed receptor then interacts with a G protein on the inner side of the membrane and causes it to release GDP and bind GTP. The GTP-bound G protein is the active form, and it goes on to activate an effector enzyme such as adenylyl cyclase, which makes the second messenger cAMP. The G protein later switches itself off by hydrolyzing GTP back to GDP.\n\n(B) is wrong because activation depends on ligand binding to the receptor, not on spontaneous activation.\n(C) is wrong because G proteins bind GTP, not ATP, and it is the receptor that triggers the exchange.\n(A) is wrong because G proteins stay associated with the membrane when they are active."
