      "explanation": "Correct: (C) χ² = 5.0, df = 3, fail to reject. Each class is expected to be 200 ÷ 4 = 50. χ² = (60 − 50)²/50 + (55 − 50)²/50 + (45 − 50)²/50 + (40 − 50)²/50 = 2.0 + 0.5 + 0.5 + 2.0 = 5.0. Four categories give df = 4 − 1 = 3, with a critical value of 7.81. Since 5.0 is below 7.81, the deviation could easily be due to chance, so we fail to reject independent assortment. (A) is wrong because it uses 1 degree of freedom; four phenotype classes give df = 3, and the correct critical value of 7.81 is not exceeded. (B) is wrong because 0.6 comes from summing |o − e| ÷ e without squaring the differences, which is not the chi-square formula. (D) is wrong because some excess of parental types is expected by chance alone, and only a statistical test can show whether 115 versus 85 is significant.",
