      "stem": "Bacteria are grown on a plate with no antibiotic, forming about 200 colonies. A velvet pad copies the positions of all colonies onto a plate containing streptomycin, where only three colonies grow. Researchers then take cells from the three matching positions on the original plate, which never contacted streptomycin, and find they are resistant; cells from other positions are not. Which conclusion is best supported?",
