      "correct": 1,
      "explanation": "Correct: (B) punctuated equilibrium. The fossil sequence shows two features of punctuated equilibrium: long stasis, with little change for millions of years, and a brief burst of change at the time a new form appears. Thirty thousand years is a short time on a geologic scale. Gradualism would instead show a smooth series of intermediate shell shapes spread through the whole sequence. (A) is wrong because gradualism predicts steady change with many intermediates through the layers, but here the shape is constant and then changes abruptly. (C) is wrong because adaptive radiation would involve one lineage splitting into many species that occupy different niches, but the data show only one shell shape being replaced by another. (D) is wrong because convergent evolution involves unrelated lineages, and these fossils come from a single lineage, so the data do not show independent origins of similar traits.",
